### Doctor Calendar API Test
### This file tests the calendar endpoint for doctors

### First, get a doctor token by logging in (replace with actual credentials)
# @name doctorLogin
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "doctor@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Store the token for subsequent requests
@token = {{doctorLogin.response.body.data.token}}

### Test Calendar API - Get December 2024 bookings for the doctor
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/appointments/calendar?year=2024&month=12
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### Test Calendar API - Get January 2025 bookings for the doctor
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/appointments/calendar?year=2025&month=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### Test Calendar API - Invalid year (should return error)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/appointments/calendar?year=2025&month=13
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### Test Calendar API - Missing parameters (should return error)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/appointments/calendar
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json